  "interpretation": "median_element_content is the fraction of a positive training window that is actually element. Where it is low, the model learned that size class from mostly-host examples, which predicts weak smeared signal -- the observed 0.857 recall / 0.334 IoU at 5-8 kb. elements_with_zero_windows counts elements that generated no positive training example at all. Either finding argues for variable-length training windows so a short window can sit inside a short element; a high-content, well-populated small stratum would instead point at an architectural cause and make downstream multi-scale the right fix."
